          "description": [
            "Performs SNV calling on a bam file."
          ],
          "documentation": [
            {
              "content": "\n\n**What it does**\n\nThis tool uses the SNVMix model (Goya et al) to call single nucleotide variants (SNVs) from a bam file.  The various models described in the study are provided (e.g. SNVMix1, MB, Mb etc.).  The most commonly-used models are MB (the default) and SNVMix1.  The former thresholds on base quality and mapping quality and uses both qualities in the variant prediction while the latter filters on both and only uses the allele counts in the model.  The output is a tab-delimited file that should be passed through the accompanying filtering script prior to use.  \n\n  ",
              "type": "help",
              "url": null
            }
          ],
